// The Mirror Pool (Pool_2; character-bibles.md §5). Marrow's one echo in Act 2: a grey chick in the reflection and
// not on the bank. It says back Wren's own last chosen line, in her words. Nothing else. Marrow's lines are copies;
// the #echo tag keeps localisation identical.

title: MirrorPool_Marrow
---
<<if has_flag("marrow.seen_in_pool")>>
    Pool: Only Wren in the water now, in colour. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pool: Water flat as paper. Wren in it, in colour.
Pool: Behind her, in the water, a grey chick. On the bank behind her, nothing.
-> Who's there?
    Marrow: Who's there? #echo:wren
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
-> You're not on the bank.
    Marrow: Not on the bank. #echo:wren
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
-> ...
    Marrow: ... #echo:wren
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
Pool: A ripple. The chick is gone. The water shows only her.
<<flag marrow.seen_in_pool 1>>
===
